language 0.1.0
module runtime
  means
    The actual execution of software components: instances existing in time,
    processes, threads, executions, states and the resources they consume.

entity instance : thing
  means
    instance: a particular embodiment of a component or other executable type,
    existing in time.

entity process : thing
  means
    process: an isolated context of program execution with resources allotted
    to it.

entity thread : thing
  means
    thread: a sequence of executed instructions within a process.

entity execution : thing
  means
    execution: a single occurrence of an operation, task or component being
    run in a definite temporal context.

entity state : thing
  means
    state: the significant properties of an instance at a definite moment in
    time.

entity transition : thing
  means
    transition: an admissible change of an instance from one state to another.

entity resource : thing
  means
    resource: a limited available entity consumed or occupied during
    execution.
